WEBVTT

00:07:58.923 --> 00:08:01.419
Do people deserve to die
for the crimes they commit?,

00:08:01.443 --> 00:08:03.305
but: Do we deserve to kill?

00:08:03.779 --> 00:08:04.987
I mean, it's fascinating.

00:08:05.011 --> 00:08:07.519
Death penalty in America
is defined by error.

00:08:07.543 --> 00:08:09.687
For every nine people
who have been executed,

00:08:09.711 --> 00:08:11.909
we've actually identified
one innocent person

00:08:11.933 --> 00:08:14.867
who's been exonerated
and released from death row.

00:08:15.494 --> 00:08:17.805
A kind of astonishing error rate --

00:08:17.829 --> 00:08:20.285
one out of nine people, innocent.

00:08:20.888 --> 00:08:22.726
I mean, it's fascinating.

00:08:22.750 --> 00:08:25.407
In aviation, we would never
let people fly on airplanes

00:08:25.431 --> 00:08:27.408
if, for every nine planes that took off,

00:08:27.432 --> 00:08:28.582
one would crash.

00:08:28.606 --> 00:08:29.607
(Laughter)

00:08:29.631 --> 00:08:32.952
But somehow, we can insulate ourselves
from this problem.